.TH SCOUR 1 "October 2026" "scour 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scour \- inspect, redact and verify PDF documents offline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scour
.I command
.RI [ file ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scour
reads a PDF without trusting a viewer, reports what the file still contains
beyond what the page shows, removes selected text and hidden data, and verifies
its own output. It has no network code, no telemetry and no runtime
dependencies.
.PP
A scrub is a full rewrite: text is removed from the content streams and the
document is serialized from its reachable object graph with a fresh
cross-reference table. Earlier revisions, orphaned objects and stale metadata
are not written.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inspect \fIfile\fR
Report metadata, hidden text, annotations, embedded files, actions, structure,
PII and integrity. Options:
.BR \-\-json ,
.BR \-\-no\-pii ,
.BR \-\-fail\-on " " N .
.TP
.B scrub \fIfile\fR \-o \fIout\fR
Remove targets and sanitize the file. Options:
.BR \-\-term " " TEXT ,
.BR \-\-pii ,
.BR \-\-pages " " LIST ,
.BR \-\-rect " " PAGE:X0,Y0,X1,Y1 ,
.BR \-\-no\-boxes ,
.BR \-\-keep\-metadata ,
.BR \-\-keep\-annotations ,
.BR \-\-keep\-attachments ,
.BR \-\-keep\-scripts ,
.BR \-\-no\-redact ,
.BR \-\-in\-place ,
.BR \-\-compress .
.TP
.B verify \fIfile\fR
Re-extract the document and report whether a target survives. Options:
.BR \-\-term " " TEXT ,
.BR \-\-pii ,
.BR \-\-pages " " LIST ,
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B tui \fIfile\fR
Interactive dashboard. Options:
.BR \-\-theme " " midnight|paper ,
.BR \-\-dump " " WIDTHxHEIGHT ,
.BR \-\-ansi ,
.BR \-\-keys " " STR .
.TP
.B text \fIfile\fR
Print the extracted text layer. Option:
.BR \-\-page " " N .
.TP
.B split \fIfile\fR
Write a page subset with
.B \-\-pages
or one file per page with
.BR \-\-each .
.TP
.B merge \-o \fIout\fR \fIa.pdf b.pdf\fR ...
Concatenate documents. Annotations and links are remapped.
.TP
.B rotate \fIfile\fR \-\-by \fIDEGREES\fR
Add a rotation to pages. Option:
.BR \-\-pages .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-password \fIPASSWORD\fR
Open an encrypted PDF. Without a usable password the command exits 3.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Output file or directory.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Print help for the command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color. The
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable has the same effect.
.SH PAGE LISTS
Pages are 1-based. A list may contain numbers and ranges separated by commas:
.BR 1 ,
.BR 1-3 ,
.BR 7,9-11 ,
.BR 5- ,
.BR \-3 .
Values are clamped to the document and de-duplicated.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; nothing remained to report.
.TP
.B 1
Findings remain: the risk is at or above the threshold, or a target survived
scrub/verify.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
The input could not be opened, decrypted or parsed.
.TP
.B 4
The output could not be written or a writer/verification failure occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
scour inspect brief.pdf
scour inspect brief.pdf --json --fail-on 10
scour scrub brief.pdf -o brief.safe.pdf --pii --term "Project Bluebird"
scour verify brief.safe.pdf --pii --term "Project Bluebird"
scour tui brief.pdf
scour text brief.pdf --page 2
scour split report.pdf --pages 1-3 -o intro.pdf
scour merge -o combined.pdf a.pdf b.pdf
scour rotate scan.pdf --by 90 -o upright.pdf
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
Text inside images is not OCR'd. Optional content layers are not modeled as
hidden. Rewriting invalidates signatures. Verification proves that the
requested targets are absent from the extracted text layer; it does not prove
that no pixel contains them, and it is not a compliance certification.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation in
.I docs/
and the project README.
